<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Fullscreen on NaiNai</title><link>https://npujol.github.io/en/tags/fullscreen/</link><description>Recent Posts in Fullscreen on NaiNai</description><generator>Hugo 0.163.3</generator><language>en-GB</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 23:42:20 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://npujol.github.io/en/tags/fullscreen/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Authoring Fullscreen Content</title><link>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-fullscreen-content/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Nainai</dc:creator><guid>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-fullscreen-content/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="fullscreen-content"&gt;Fullscreen Content&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fullscreen pages display content without any header, footer, or navigation elements. They occupy the entire viewport.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="creating-fullscreen-pages"&gt;Creating Fullscreen Pages&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;type: 'fullscreen'&lt;/code&gt; in your frontmatter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;fullscreen&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Fullscreen Page Title&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Your&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="use-cases"&gt;Use Cases&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fullscreen pages are ideal for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Presentations&lt;/strong&gt; — Display content without distractions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Showcases&lt;/strong&gt; — Highlight specific work or projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Articles&lt;/strong&gt; — Focus readers on the content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gallery pages&lt;/strong&gt; — Display images without UI elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="fullscreen-example"&gt;Fullscreen Example&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A fullscreen page can contain any valid Markdown or HTML content. The theme ensures the content is properly centered and readable.&lt;/p&gt;</description><content:encoded>&lt;h2 id="fullscreen-content"&gt;Fullscreen Content&lt;/h2&gt;
